Kim Hunter wrote:

> 
> Can a DEC Multia (UDB 166) run Open VMS or Digital Unix.
> I know it will run Windows NT - good.

My signature aside, I can say that the OpenVMS answer is no.  To get a 100%
official Digital answer, you'd have to talk to a product manager, which I'm not.
I am a person who has written actual bits in the OpenVMS boot path, and so far
as I know, no firmware support ever appeared to make a Multia boot OpenVMS.
Hence, Multias do not possess the know-how to load the OpenVMS primary bootstrap.
Big obstacle to running OpenVMS.

--
Me, Not Digital

David F. Wall (Digital Equipment Corp., Nashua, NH)
Internet        wall@rndhse.enet.dec.com
