In article <32B96224.424D@thymenagain.com>, Kim Hunter
<kim@thymenagain.com> writes:
:I heard rumor that netscape has a webserver that runs on open vms. Is
:this true, and if so, where do ya get this?

  It's no rumor.  There are multiple webservers available (for OpenVMS
  VAX and for OpenVMS Alpha), including both commercial (licensed) and
  non-commercial packages.  Commercial webservers are available for
  OpenVMS (VAX and Alpha) from Netscape, Purveyor, and various other
  vendors.  The non-commercial packages include the OSU web server,
  among other packages.

  The Netscape server binaries are available as part of the OpenVMS
  (VAX and Alpha) V7.1 distribution -- the Internet Products Suite (IPS)
  CD-ROM kit is also available seperately.  The commercial packages on
  the IPS kit include `test drive' licenses.  (Subscription customers
  should be seeing the V7.1 distribution kits arriving in January.)

  Early copies (V1.0?) of the IPS CD-ROM were available at the Anaheim
  Fall 1996 DECUS, with the Netscape servers first appearing on the
  just-current (V1.1?) release.

