I have a customer who runs a defrag prgram that I was told by this
customer that comes with VMS 6.1. He has just added a Seagate ST32171N
drive (2.1GB) drive that seems to function fine under normal
circumstances. He started running a this Defrag program in the middle
of the night and has noticed that the program chokes when attempting to
Defrag this drive. I don't have the specifics of the actual error from
the errorlog, but the problems refer to "scsi bus phase error, phase
change timeout on scsi bus b during data in", and "command transmission
error- fatal controller error", and "inconsistent I/O data base", and
unexpected interrupts and fatal bugcheck which crached the system.
These symptoms only occured during the defragmentation process. This
system has been rock solid under all other operations. The drive also
had "QIO error on move file" for that particular volume (DKB200),
during the failure. If you have experienced a similar problem I would
like to hear from you. A fix would be great.
Thanks in advance for any suggestions/recomendations,
Dan in Maryland



