Some of the Seagates have what I consider an odd sort of tagged command
queue support, but VMS 6.1 doesn't use that. It may however be that
such a disk is subject to some rate intensive problems. I'd see if there
is more recent firmware for such a thing. Command transmission errors are
sometimes due to devices having this kind of problem. this is just a
guess, but with no error log info or similar drives available to me to
look at it makes it kinda hard to divine what may be really going on.




